    "title": "Minneapolis Mayor Allocates $150,000 to Aid Food Shelves Amid SNAP Uncertainty Due to Federal Shutdown - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Zach White ,\n1 days ago As a federal shutdown brings uncertainty to SNAP benefits, Minneapolis Mayor Jacob Frey is stepping in to mitigate potential fallout, the City of Minneapolis reports. The mayor recently directed $150,000 to support local nonprofit partners that offer free, nutritious food, an aid to the 60,000 Minneapolis residents relying on SNAP. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
